Bark's server (captaind) 0.7.1, commit 8f5d8c4f: a Lightning receive can commit
its invoice to a description hash.

StartLightningReceiveRequest gains `optional bytes description_hash = 1000`
(numbered far from upstream's own fields). When a client sends it, captaind
asks the hold plugin for an invoice whose BOLT11 `h` field is that hash, in
place of a memo (the plugin already takes `Description::Hash`). An LNURL-pay
service (a Lightning address) needs this: LUD-06 as first written had the
payer check that the invoice's description hash is sha256 of the metadata it
was served, and payers that still make that check refuse an invoice that
does not commit to it. The current LUD-06 text no longer asks for the check.

It only adds. A request without the field is handled exactly as before; a
request with both a description and a hash, or a hash that is not 32 bytes, is
refused as an invalid argument. A server without this patch ignores the field
and makes the invoice without a hash, which the Arca wallet library detects
and refuses. The struct literals of upstream's own client and tests gain
`description_hash: None` so the tree still builds.

Applies to a clean checkout of 8f5d8c4f with `git apply`, before or after
bark-testnet4.patch and bark-reorg-repair.patch.

